{"body":"I solved the cash register problem using .NET Core 2.0 API with a Swagger client. I hope it works well for you!\r\n\r\nCheck out the README for instructions on how to run the demo and special considerations regarding the extensible business logic. The application supports 2/3 of the additional use cases (configurable currencies, configurable divisor). If the requirement was to support multiple concurrent currencies, we could add a currency indicator to the input file and limit the denominations dictionary based on the indicator for each line in the input.\r\n\r\nFor the third additional use case, I suspect that we could add some third-party Domain Specific Language to allow for custom formulas to dictate business logic by configuration, or perhaps some sort of plugin system to support the application long term.\r\n\r\nPlease let me know your feedback and if you would have approached it differently. I'm particularly curious how you would have approached adding another special case. \r\n\r\nThanks!","created_at":"2018-05-22T15:23:46Z","head_ref":"master","head_repo":"dylinmaust/CashRegister","html_url":"https://github.com/TrueFit/CashRegister/pull/38","merged_at":null,"number":38,"state":"closed","title":"Cash Register Solution"}
