{"body":"Here is the code I did for your test.  I coded it using Visual Studio 2010 and it is written in visual basic.  I am also going to send the solution to the recruiting firm so that they have a copy as well.  \n","created_at":"2015-05-04T22:36:09Z","head_ref":"master","head_repo":"GeorgeMcDonald175/CashRegister","html_url":"https://github.com/TrueFit/CashRegister/pull/17","merged_at":null,"number":17,"state":"closed","title":"Code test for George McDonald"}
{"body":"I did this code test using a single page of html with JavaScript and JQuery to run the code.  This allows it to fit into a larger solution but also gives the possibility to just output the data to a file instead of displaying on the page like it is now.\n\nFor such a small project I thought that the single page solution would work best.  I'm an experienced web developer so I gravitate toward a browser based solution.  Only client side code was really needed in this case, though I have more experience using C# .Net I decided against it for this demo.\n\nFor this demo I did get to learn a bit more JavaScript than I had used in the past.  For example I had the idea I wanted to use a dictionary for the currency denominations but had to look to see if JavaScript actually had that capability.  Also, one other thing I learned from this that I will use going forward is that Sublime Text makes a nice IDE for HTML and JavaScript based solutions.\n","created_at":"2015-05-01T03:46:19Z","head_ref":"master","head_repo":"jchadman/CashRegister","html_url":"https://github.com/TrueFit/CashRegister/pull/16","merged_at":null,"number":16,"state":"closed","title":"Create CreativeCashDrawSolutionsRegister"}
